<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 90,265 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 90,265 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 90,265 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday compared to 81,113 tonnes in the same period on Monday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Tuesday     April 14</p>
<p>    Export cargo		10,369	11,735</p>
<p>    Import cargo		79,896	69,378</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, four ship sailed and three berthed. In the next 24 hours, six are expected to sail and eight are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Tallow		    6,000	 Ocean Mag	    16/4</p>
<p>Sugar		    12,163	 Feng Sheng	   17/4</p>
<p>Containers		  555	 CMBT Himalaya	23/4</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
